# Job: Core — a ROUTER requester must accept the reply on the current same-RID Completion pipe (reply pair-mismatch discard)

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. One cause, Core-owned, hard: take the time to get
the invariant right (cap 2 h). Work ONLY in the isolated worktree `/home/hep7/project/zlink-core-fix`
(detached HEAD at current main). Read `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.ko.md` §3-§5, and
`core/doc/spec/core/systems/10-hot-path.ko.md` §3 (forbidden list) first.

## Established facts (verified by the supervisor, do not re-derive)
- Pure-C repro `doc/plan/c016-worklog/tools/repro_router_reply_pair_mismatch.cpp` (in the worktree)
  fails 5/5 and 3/3: two ROUTERs with explicit RIDs, caller binds and connects FIRST while the owner is
  not yet bound (pending connect), then the owner binds and connects back (reciprocal); both sockets
  in pollers with POLLIN|POLLERR|POLLOUT|POLLCOMPLETION; Hello/Admit-style DATA both ways; caller
  `zlink_request_part` (DONTWAIT, 3 s timeout, completion id 1) → owner `zlink_router_recv_part` →
  owner replies from another thread ~50 ms later with the captured token → `zlink_reply_part` returns
  OK → caller never gets a REQUEST completion until the deadline: `request_result=101 TimedOut`.
  Control (both bind first, then connect): 25/25 OK. Build/run:
  `g++ -std=c++17 -I core/include doc/plan/c016-worklog/tools/repro_router_reply_pair_mismatch.cpp -L core/build-dev/lib -lzlink -Wl,-rpath,$PWD/core/build-dev/lib -pthread -o /tmp/repro_core_fix && /tmp/repro_core_fix` (exit 7 = fail).
- Root cause (GDB-confirmed by the previous job, see
  `doc/plan/c016-worklog/bucketB-dotnet-stale-summary.md` in the main tree
  `/home/hep7/project/zlink/doc/plan/c016-worklog/bucketB-dotnet-stale-summary.md`):
  the responder picks the *current* ready Completion pipe of the source logical RID
  (`core/src/api/socket/socket_request_reply_runtime_io.cpp:1334-1406`; captured target had
  `route_binding_token=0` so the captured Application pair was not reused), writes the reply there
  (`socket_request_reply_submit_api.cpp:459-466`) and returns OK. The caller reads that frame from its
  Completion pipe (`socket_request_reply_dispatch.cpp:269-297`) but
  `take_pending_reply_from_transport_locked()` (`socket_request_reply_pending_api.cpp:89-158`) requires
  the incoming pipe's transport pair id/generation to equal the **submit-time** pair stored in the
  pending request, returns false, and the caller silently closes the reply as
  `completion_message_accepted` (`socket_request_reply_dispatch.cpp:151-160`) — the pending request
  stays until its deadline. With two live transport pairs to the same logical peer (the reciprocal
  connect case) the reply lands on the "other" pair.
- Spec (`core/doc/spec/core/socket/07-router.ko.md` §9 raw reply submit, ~lines 285-316): the reply
  FINAL waits for "같은 logical source RID의 reply route가 local admission" and picks "현재 ready
  completion progress lane의 Completion pipe"; "Physical disconnect, connection generation 변경과
  requester timeout은 token을 무효화하지 않는다"; "requester Core는 이미 correlation이 없으면
  늦은 reply를 폐기한다". Requester-side text pins correlation to the request, NOT to a physical pair.
  Ruling D-072 (`doc/plan/c016-worklog/decisions.ko.md`): reply routes by logical RID like any send;
  Core send side already does so. So the fix is on the **receive/correlation side**: a reply arriving
  on any live Completion pipe of the same logical peer RID must complete the pending request. Do NOT
  revert the send side to the submit-time pair (that contradicts D-072), and do NOT accept "any pair"
  blindly — validate: pending request's logical target RID == source pipe's peer logical RID, source
  pipe is a live Completion-lane pipe of a ROUTER peer with an active lifecycle, and the frame's
  request_seq matches. Keep the existing exactly-once / teardown-race guarantees (the generation lock
  block at the end of that function) intact.

